#
# RX23302: all routed traffic (NAT, firewall) goes through one MIPS 24Kc core.
# Software flow offloading moves established connections to the kernel's fast
# path (nftables flowtable), bypassing most of the firewall per packet.
# Measured on the board 15.10.2026: TV stream connections land in the
# flowtable (OFFLOAD in conntrack), nothing else changes.
#
# flow_offloading_hw (29.10.2026): the hardware NAT engine of the RTL8197F is
# ported from the ADCDS DIR-842 driver (rtl865x_asichal.c + rtl819x_hwnat.c).
# The flag makes fw4 declare its flowtable with `flags offload`, so the kernel
# offers established flows to the driver (ndo_setup_tc/TC_SETUP_FT). The
# driver itself gates row programming behind /sys/module/rtl819x/parameters/hwnat
# (default 0) AND router mode (/proc/rtl819x_router=1): with the gate closed
# every offer is declined and flows stay on the software path exactly as
# before, so this setting is safe to ship even when the gate is off.

. /lib/functions.sh

[ "$(board_name)" = "electra,rx23302" ] || exit 0

uci -q get firewall.@defaults[0] >/dev/null || exit 0
uci set firewall.@defaults[0].flow_offloading='1'
uci set firewall.@defaults[0].flow_offloading_hw='1'
uci commit firewall

exit 0
